# =====================================================================
# rb4011_fixsyslog_delta — remote-syslog egress refresh-on-boot SAFETY NET
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Silent syslog usually means the TUNNEL, not RouterOS: WireGuard drops an inner
# packet whose source IP is absent from the peer's AllowedIPs, so a log sourced on
# wg-s2s dies at the VPS endpoint with no error anywhere. AllowedIPs is SSOT:
# `wg_s2s_vps.allowed_ips` (group_vars/all/).
# → docs/network-ops.md §Central log shipping — RouterOS logs → VPS CrowdSec + VictoriaLogs
#
# This script+scheduler is harmless SELF-HEALING INSURANCE: RouterOS has no
# enable/disable for a logging action, so if a boot fails to (re)init the remote
# action a startup scheduler re-applies the target once the tunnel is up
# (`start-time=startup`, `interval=0` = once; the script's :delay 10s covers bring-up).
#
# Naming rule: RouterOS 7 scheduler/script names are letters+numbers ONLY — a hyphen
# is rejected, hence `fixsyslog` (and the `centralsyslog` action).
# The toggle targets `centralsyslog`, NOT the bundled `remote` action: `remote` sits
# at 0.0.0.0 with no rules bound, so `[find name=remote]` is a silent no-op.
# The VPS target is SSOT-derived: `{{ wireguard_s2s_vps.remote_ip }}`.
# Render: playbooks/render-converge.yml; apply: scripts/routeros-apply-delta.sh.
# =====================================================================
# Script: refresh the centralsyslog action's remote target (0.0.0.0 -> real)
# Note: a single-line quoted `source=` keeps the /import parser happy.
:if ([/system script find where name=fixsyslog] = "") do={
    /system script add name=fixsyslog source=":delay 10s; /system logging action set [find name=centralsyslog] remote=0.0.0.0; :delay 1s; /system logging action set [find name=centralsyslog] remote={{ wireguard_s2s_vps.remote_ip.split('/')[0] }};"
}
# Scheduler: run the script once at startup (~3s after boot; the script's own
# :delay 10s covers wg-s2s/route bring-up). interval=0 = run once, no repeat.
:if ([/system scheduler find where name=fixsyslog] = "") do={
    /system scheduler add name=fixsyslog on-event=fixsyslog start-time=startup interval=0 policy=read,write,test
}
# =====================================================================
# Verify: /system script print, /system scheduler print, then on the next reboot check
# that the VPS collector receives routeros-syslog (`cscli alerts list`) and the wg-s2s
# sniffer:
#   /tool sniffer quick interface=wg-s2s ip-protocol=udp port=514
# → docs/network-ops.md §Central log shipping — RouterOS logs → VPS CrowdSec + VictoriaLogs
# =====================================================================